<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!-- GT_esmini verification asset (feature:F7, curve-onset repro, 2026-07-27).
     Five INDEPENDENT single-lane "town" roads (no junctions: each road is its
     own dead end), matching curve_2lane_r300.xodr's "no link" precedent for a
     self-contained test road; §B1 of the opendrive-authoring skill says a
     junction is only needed when a connection is AMBIGUOUS, and there is no
     other road here to connect to).

     Road id=0 is a straight control (0 deg). Roads id=1..4 are a 30 m straight
     lead-in followed by a 150 m constant-radius RIGHT arc (curvature < 0),
     radius chosen so the wheel EGO is teleported onto (see the companion
     f7_curve_onset_*deg.xosc scenarios) demands a specific steering-WHEEL
     rotation at the moment of the "sudden onset" teleport:

       target wheel rotation [deg] = axis_frac * 450  (scripts/ffb_spike/
         wheel_session_report.py:287 "peak*450": the established F7 axis-
         fraction -> physical-G29-degrees convention; this is the SAME 450
         deg/axis-frac used to derive "36.0 deg" from residual_threshold=0.08
         in test_results/f7_residual_handoff_C.md Sec.5-6, and is what the
         user's real-machine "30 deg" report (Sec.5-4/Sec.6-3, ==0.0667
         axis-frac) is stated in).
       axis_frac = wheel_deg / 450
       tire delta = axis_frac * max_steer_angle(0.61 rad, GT_esmini/config/
         virtual_driver.json:22)                       [bicycle-model steer,
         vd_resume_transient.py kinematic_window_metrics: delta = sn*MAX_STEER_ANGLE]
       kappa = tan(delta) / wheel_base(3.0 m = car_white bbox length 5.0 in
         decelerate_for_left_turn.xosc * 0.6, ControllerVirtualDriver.cpp:312)
       R = 1 / kappa

     Table (see f7_curve_onset_repro.md for the full derivation):
       road id=1  wheel_deg=10  axis_frac=0.02222  tire_delta=0.777 deg  R=221.298 m
       road id=2  wheel_deg=20  axis_frac=0.04444  tire_delta=1.553 deg  R=110.629 m
       road id=3  wheel_deg=30  axis_frac=0.06667  tire_delta=2.330 deg  R=73.730  m
       road id=4  wheel_deg=45  axis_frac=0.10000  tire_delta=3.495 deg  R=49.119  m

     NOTE ON THE fabriksgatan_traffic_lights.xodr JUNCTION TURNS (road 13, R~9.25 m,
     used unmodified by decelerate_for_left_turn.xosc / traffic_lights_junction.xosc):
     those correspond to wheel_deg ~= 231 (axis_frac ~= 0.514) by this SAME formula,
     a much more extreme demand than the user's cited "30 deg". They remain useful as
     a large-signal sanity check but must NOT be labeled against the 0/10/20/30/45 deg
     scale without the conversion above (tire-angle-normalized vs wheel-rotation-
     normalized axis fractions are NOT the same number: see the ratio-confusion
     precedent this project already hit once on OSI HVD steering_angle, ~12.9x).

     Lane layout copied from fabriksgatan_traffic_lights.xodr road id=3 (town street,
     single driving lane each way + border + sidewalk) for a "gentle everyday road"
     flavor consistent with the user's real-machine bug report (not a tight junction). -->
<OpenDRIVE>
